republic-overreach.md:1: argue/readings: S1 is read 2 ways: republic-overreach.logic.r2 has "¬exceeds_like(just) ∧ exceeds_unlike(just) ∧ exceeds_like(unjust) ∧ exceeds_unlike(unjust)"; republic-overreach.logic.r2.2 and republic-overreach.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; they differ when only "just desires (claims) to have more than, or go beyond, his like" is true, which the second allows
republic-overreach.md:1: argue/answered: S1: answered no, which keeps republic-overreach.logic.r2, to: Suppose "just desires (claims) to have more than, or go beyond, his like" is true and "unjust desires (claims) to have more than, or go beyond, his like", "just desires (claims) to have more than, or go beyond, his unlike" and "unjust desires (claims) to have more than, or go beyond, his unlike" are false. Is S1, "We may put the matter thus, I said—the just does not desire more than his like but more than his unlike, whereas the unjust desires more than both his like and his unlike?", true then?
